  "body": "If we could somehow get to a state where all browsers on all platforms could properly isolate sites as needed (using processes as things stand today), it might be nice if COOP could become an optional aspect of cross-origin isolated?\r\n\r\nTo get there, it seems COEP could reuse the mechanism from https://github.com/WICG/origin-isolation (as well as resulting semantics) to store \"require-corp\" as the policy for an origin for the lifetime of a browsing context group.\r\n\r\nI don't think we're anywhere near there today, but we could retrofit COEP in anticipation of that occurring at some point in the future and also give it some additional benefits \"today\".\r\n\r\n(This also makes me wonder what kind of other policies one might wish to enforce for an origin within a browsing context group. I could see other things making use of this as well.)",
